WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.160
Your rhythm's kinda off.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:02.940
Huh?

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:08.770
Maybe try the windup instead of the set.
Should make it easier to find your rhythm.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:10.740
It'll be okay.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.450
They won't be able to hit your fastballs,

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:14.860
even if they're down the pipe.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.870
Just trust in yourself
and throw it at my mitt.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.330
Strike three!

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.750
Hell yeah!

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:28.840
Yeah!

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.840
This fella ain't bad after all.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.010
<i>Just one more.</i>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.300
<i>If they're only two ahead, there's still hope!</i>

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.550
<i>Please, Nishina!</i>

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.810
<i>Please get us through this!</i>

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.810
Andy, finish it!

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.940
Strike! You're out!

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:52.690
All right! We survived!

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.960
We have three outs left.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.210
It's only two runs.
We can make that up in one go!

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.630
Let's not give up until the very end!

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.130
Fuurin, fight!

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:37.420
<b>Last Inning</b>

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:36.050
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:36.050
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:36.050
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.620
Yeah!

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.790
<i>Bottom of the seventh.</i>

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.970
<i>Fuurin Academy to bat.</i>

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:48.340
<i>Batting third, second base, Sawa-san.</i>

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.980
Get on base! On base!

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.400
Come on, Yayoi!

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.040
Play!

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.280
<i>Three more outs.</i>

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.940
<i>We'll win this and move on to
tomorrow's semifinal and final.</i>

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.120
Strike!

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:23.430
<i>Good. Looks like Urabe's kicked 
it up a notch for the last inning.</i>

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.690
All right!

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.470
We got a runner on base with no outs!

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:47.110
<i>Batting fourth, left field, Kabashima-san.</i>

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.080
Anita!

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.040
Go for it!

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.510
Oh, yeah. Anita's right hand is injured.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.060
Yeah.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.810
Strike!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:22.830
<i>My wrist's hurtin', but now ain't
the time to be thinkin' 'bout that.</i>

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.860
<i>Startin' with the two runs
in the first innin',</i>

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:30.460
<i>them takin' the lead, and then 
widenin' the gap even more...</i>

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:31.910
<i>All of that was my fault!</i>

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.080
Strike two!

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.040
Both pitches went inside.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:42.260
If one went outside, she'd have
a chance to adjust and swing one-handed,

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:47.970
so they're aiming inside, where it's hard
for Anita because of her injured hand!

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.710
There's no way she can hit those.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:59.230
<i>Her only chance is to gamble
and go all-in on one swing.</i>

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:00.650
<i>But right now...</i>

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:04.530
<i>I don't know if Anita's capable of picking up
on the battery focusing down her inside.</i>

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.870
<i>Don't hold back, Urabe.</i>

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.090
<i>If that's how yer gonna play it...</i>

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.080
Now it's right over the plate!

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.570
She did it!

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:36.340
Oh, man! So close!

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:37.640
Keep going!

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:42.640
All right!

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.900
No outs, runners on second and third!

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.950
<i>Anita came up with a plan after all.</i>

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:53.010
<i>Her right hand's banged up pretty bad,
but that was an amazing hit!</i>

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.910
Let's keep it going!

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.880
<i>Batting fifth, right field, Sakura-san.</i>

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:01.150
This is insane.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.050
One good hit and we're tied?!

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.520
<i>Don't squeeze.</i>

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:09.800
<i>Put the ball in play and bring a runner home.</i>

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.050
Play!

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.520
Dammit.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:21.080
<i>We can't afford to lose in this round!</i>

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.650
<i>We set our goals for this year
way higher than this!</i>

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.110
Strike!

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:33.090
<i>If we lose to this random co-ed team,</i>

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:38.040
<i>there's no way we'll beat Eihou!</i>

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:39.860
Strike!

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:41.170
You're out!

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:50.530
I'm sorry...

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:55.100
<i>Batting sixth, third base, Kandori-san.</i>

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.890
Calm down, Kandori!

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:59.540
Like that's gonna help.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:03.860
Someone please tell me why
she's higher in the lineup than me.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:13.580
Kandori...

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.010
Yes!

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:21.000
Strike three! You're out!

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.670
I'm so sorry.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:25.070
We squandered our chance.

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:31.290
<i>Batting seventh, pitcher, Nishina-kun.</i>

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.350
Nishina!

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.560
Get us something!

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.520
<i>Please, Nishina.</i>

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.060
<i>Just one more!</i>

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.770
<i>If I get you out, it's over!</i>

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:50.400
He got it!

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:53.360
Fall in!

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:55.120
Foul!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.250
So close!

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:05.330
<i>Damn. That woulda been perfect.</i>

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:10.490
<i>P-Please!</i>

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:14.080
<i>If nothing else, let Nishina
 tie the game for us!</i>

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:17.300
Ball!

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:21.340
<i>Actually, I wouldn't even mind 
if the game ended with Nishina.</i>

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:27.270
<i>Anything but me being the 
last in to bat in this game!</i>

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.230
Ball!

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:32.620
<i>We don't need to fight this guy.</i>

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:38.780
<i>We've struck the next guy out twice in a row.
We're guaranteed to get him out again.</i>

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:42.140
I guess that hit before spooked them?

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:45.040
First base is open, too.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:49.000
But ol' Tanba's up next.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.460
Ball three!

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:54.260
Come on, you coward!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.180
Throw me a strike!

00:08:58.490 --> 00:08:59.500
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.520
<i>Doing whatever it takes 
to win is not cowardice!</i>

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.480
Ball four!

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.190
<i>Yes, correct call.</i>

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:10.510
Dammit.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:12.980
Shoulda got it on the first pitch.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:15.240
Mr. Hasn't-Got-It.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.980
<i>Batting eighth, first base, Tanba-kun.</i>

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:27.310
Is he... doing the robot?

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:29.110
I don't think this is going to work.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:34.300
Daigo! Shouldn't you call a 
timeout and go calm him down?

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:37.260
He's going to end the game
without doing anything.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:05.480
<i>Yamazaki pitched yesterday.
Why's he warming up?</i>

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:09.780
<i>Why do they want him to get ready?!</i>

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:16.720
Ball!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.300
<i>I'm the ace, Coach!</i>

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:26.850
<i>Is that how much faith you have in me?!</i>

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:28.560
Ball!

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.520
<i>What's wrong, Urabe?</i>

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:33.940
Nice, nice!

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:36.650
Good eye, Tanba-senpai!

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:39.860
<i>He's nervous, but he's
still seeing them clearly.</i>

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:42.530
Ball!

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:49.230
<i>You might not have overcome the trauma
of losing that game for the team.</i>

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:54.020
<i>But you're not that Tanba-san anymore.</i>

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:00.380
Tanba-san.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:03.180
Let's pick at least one of
those pitches to swing at.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.460
You never know. You might get lucky.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.070
I can't believe it!

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:27.620
<i>All right! We win!</i>

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.160
<i>Suck on this!</i>

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:30.370
Urabe!

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:37.630
Safe!

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.590
Safe!

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:44.640
Yes!

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:45.760
4-3!

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.430
We got one run back!

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.870
It's a miracle.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.890
Nice one, Senpai!

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.350
So that's a Mr. Has-Got-It.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:59.360
Looks like the tides are turning our way.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.200
<b>Nishina</b>

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.200
<b>Tanba</b>

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.200
<b>Shigeno</b>

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:12.200
<i>Batting ninth, catcher, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:19.000
<i>Shi-ge-no!</i>

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:21.770
<i>Looks like it's you and me, Urabe!</i>

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:35.850
<i>Last inning.</i>

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:39.580
<i>4-3.</i>

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:46.140
<i>Two outs, bases loaded.</i>

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.660
Hit it, Daigo!

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:53.080
<i>I don't think so!</i>

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.130
<i>Shigeno!</i>

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:24.270
<i>Urabe!</i>

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:26.520
I'm sorry.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:29.830
I don't need apologies.

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:32.530
Just keep learning the ropes.

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:35.290
As catcher, you've got so much 
to do and to think about,

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.190
you don't have time to get down on yourself.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.460
<i>I'm </i>definitely<i> hitting this!</i>

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:43.670
<i>I'll </i>never<i> let you hit it!</i>

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.500
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.450
<i>His timing is good,
 and he's got a precise swing.</i>

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:02.150
<i>He got in a good hit to 
center field last time, too.</i>

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:04.530
<i>Coming at him with
fastballs is too dangerous.</i>

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.620
<i>It doesn't have to be in the strike zone.</i>

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.490
<i>Just mess up his timing with a curveball.</i>

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:10.720
<i>What?!</i>

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:12.870
<i>I won't let you hit it!</i>

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.250
Foul!

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:19.210
That was so close!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:20.920
Timeout!

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:22.450
Timeout!

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:29.970
<i>He's got a good swing.</i>

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:34.350
<i>How much d'ya hafta swing 
a bat to get a swing like that?</i>

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:40.400
<i>I've been doubtin' Shigeno-senpai 
ever since I joined the team.</i>

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:47.690
<i>How could the smallest guy
on the team be captain?</i>

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:51.290
<i>He handed the startin'
catcher position to me,</i>

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:55.780
<i>so I figured he was captain in name only,
 with zero confidence or skill.</i>

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.030
<i>I could'na been more wrong.</i>

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:07.980
Play!

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:10.090
<i>Shigeno-senpai...</i>

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:13.550
<i>As a catcher...</i>

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:20.350
<i>As a captain...</i>

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:27.460
<i>He's always thinkin' 'bout the 
next step for the team as a whole!</i>

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.750
Foul! Foul!

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.460
So <i>close</i>.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:51.920
Dammit. Why are they readying Yamazaki?

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:55.220
We may have two outs, but bases
are loaded and we're only one ahead.

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:57.890
Considering this may go into extra innings,

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:01.360
it's only natural Coach wants
our relief pitcher ready to play.

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:05.210
It's not that Coach doesn't have faith in you.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:10.320
I understand you really wanting to get 
Shigeno out, but you need to cool it.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.840
You get it, right?

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.340
Shigeno's got a read on your fastballs.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:20.340
It doesn't matter if you throw balls, 
just pitch him some nice curveballs.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.750
If you keep throwing the same pitch,
he will hit it.

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:26.610
But I can't control the curveballs.

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:31.910
We can't afford a wild pitch 
when the bases are loaded.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.060
I won't let them past me!

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:35.940
I promise I'll stop them!

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:38.510
So stop worrying and throw 
the best curveballs you can!

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:45.330
<i>Since I told him that, the accuracy
and spin on his curveballs has come back.</i>

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:46.630
<i>Another one.</i>

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:48.940
<i>Shigeno's not ready for your curveballs.</i>

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:58.340
<i>Daigo!</i>

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:18.110
Get it, Moriguchi!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.220
We did it!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:24.290
We caught up!

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:26.480
Back home!

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:00.390
Safe!

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:12.270
Bow!

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:14.230
Good game!

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:21.780
Urabe...

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:30.640
Please give him space, Shigeno.

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:36.690
Sorry.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:52.810
I'm really sorry, Coach.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:57.950
You were readying Yamazaki,
but they got a hit before he could come in.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:00.490
Don't sweat it.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.110
But, sir...

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:05.580
Whatever happened,

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:09.980
I was never going to swap out my ace
until the seventh inning wrapped up.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:16.570
I know this is hard to take.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:20.340
But next summer will
roll around soon enough.

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:24.830
Let's get stronger so we can
pay them back next time.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:27.320
Y-Yes, sir!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:37.280
Mifune Baseball Park

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:37.280
Mifune Baseball Park

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:34.040
But boy, what a surprise.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:36.730
I didn't think you'd make a comeback.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:41.020
Congratulations. This is so great.

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:45.240
Now we can come back here again tomorrow.

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:50.150
Could she sound any less enthusiastic?

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:51.240
All right, then, Sensei.

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:53.480
We'll see you again tomorrow.

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:58.520
We're sticking around for the next game,
but you can go on home.

00:19:58.520 --> 00:19:59.890
Thanks for everything.

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:01.630
Oh, really? Bye, then.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.200
Look at her go!

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:07.950
Hey, Daigo, why are we watching the next game?

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:08.570
Huh?

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:14.470
You already watched our
next opponent early this morning.

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:16.160
Oh, right.

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:19.970
Our next opponent.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Tokumei</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Tokumei</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Atsumori</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Atsumori</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Haragase</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Haragase</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Nishi-
Minato</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Nishi-
Minato</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Nakahama</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Nakahama</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Yanagawa</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Yanagawa</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Itsuki</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Fuurin</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Fuurin</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Koutou</b>

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:28.660
<b>Koutou</b>

