00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:39.180
Eihou?

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:42.700
C'mon, Daigo, what's the point of watching them?

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:46.800
You <i>do</i> know they're district
champs every year, right?

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:49.760
Of course. That's why we're 
going to check them out.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:56.880
From what I saw this morning,

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:00.370
we have a good chance
of beating Yanagawa Middle.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:05.000
To be honest, they're quite a bit weaker 
than Itsuki Middle and Seiwa Middle,

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:07.070
and we already beat them.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:08.570
They won't be a difficult opponent.

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:13.130
Since it's all but guaranteed
that Eihou will make it to the final,

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:16.290
we will have to fight them
right around this time tomorrow,

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:21.500
Even if it's a game we can't win,
I'd like to put up the best fight we can.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.550
<b>Fujimihara</b>

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.550
<b>Fujimihara</b>

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.550
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.550
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:30.240
<i>Top of the first.</i>

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.520
<i>Fujimihara Middle to bat.</i>

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:36.480
<i>Batting first, right field, Fukazawa-kun.</i>

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:38.950
Where are Tao and the others?

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.680
They said they needed the bathroom.

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:42.840
All three of them?

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:46.490
<i>So that's Eihou's ace, huh?</i>

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:49.890
<i>He sure is tall.</i>

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:01.710
Strike!

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:03.900
That was fast as spit! Unbelievable!

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:05.940
That had to be around 140 kmph!

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:10.090
<i>Right. So that's why they're
back-to-back district champs.</i>

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:11.520
Um...

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:17.470
So, uh... Sagara-senpai
and Sawa-senpai went home.

00:22:17.470 --> 00:22:20.100
They said, "Good luck, Daigo-kyun."

00:24:00.400 --> 00:24:03.350
Mutsuko-chan, congrats on winning
your second-round game!

00:24:03.350 --> 00:24:06.640
It's all thanks to the breaking 
balls you taught me, Izumi-senpai!

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:10.410
But can tomorrow's semi-finals 
even go ahead in this weather?

00:24:10.410 --> 00:24:13.220
We've all got to think about tomorrow.

00:24:13.630 --> 00:24:15.760
As the pitcher, I've got my own doubts...

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:17.760
C'mon! Chin up!

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:20.020
Hey, Daigo! You're the captain! Say something!

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>Cloudy, Then Rainy?</b>

00:24:20.410 --> 00:24:22.720
Next time: "Cloudy, Then Rainy?"

00:24:22.720 --> 00:24:25.020
Run to the stage of your dreams!
